2) If by "all the structures" you mean "all the
binary structures for all the runtime environments",
you can reduce your problem size significantly by
picking some common (say text) intermediate format,
writing to it, reading from it, thereby cutting down
an O(environments^2) problem to an O(environments)
problem.

That intermediate format could then become the
Hearse format for transport and storage, and all
existing Hearse files (at least for 3.4.3) be ported
to it.


